\chapter{Enum Reflection}\label{ch29-enum-reflection}

\texttt{MuDSL.\allowbreak{}hpp} embeds the complete public header API of
\href{https://github.com/Neargye/magic_enum/tree/v0.9.8}{magic\_enum
v0.9.8}: core reflection, flags, utility functions, fusion, constexpr
switch dispatch, containers, stream operators, and formatting. It
remains a self-contained C++20 header; no magic\_enum installation or
link dependency is required.

The D module provides the same core reflection capability through native
enum member discovery: names, values, entries, casts, indexing,
adjacency, flags, compile-time dispatch/fusion and enum-indexed
containers. Its customization uses \texttt{EnumOptions} and
\texttt{EnumNames} UDAs, with no numeric search interval. Chapter 31
(Chapter 31) documents the D API and the language-specific differences.
This chapter covers the embedded C++ API.

\section{Namespaces and feature
composition}\label{ch29-namespaces-and-feature-composition}

Reflection functions and traits are exposed directly in
\texttt{dsl:\allowbreak{}:\allowbreak{}} with using declarations. These
declarations preserve the upstream overloads, template parameters,
return types, \texttt{constexpr}, and \texttt{noexcept} behavior.

The entire API is also available through
\texttt{dsl:\allowbreak{}:\allowbreak{}enum\_\allowbreak{}reflection},
which aliases
\texttt{:\allowbreak{}:\allowbreak{}magic\_\allowbreak{}enum}. Namespace
aliases expose the other public facilities:

