Flags reflection enumerates named individual power-of-two bits,
including high bits of unsigned underlying types. Zero and named
composite constants are excluded from the flags value list. Zero is not
a valid flag combination; unknown bits also fail validation. Global
numeric range macros do not limit the flags scan.

\texttt{bitwise\_\allowbreak{}operators} contains
\texttt{\textasciitilde{}}, \texttt{|}, \texttt{\&},
\texttt{\textasciicircum{}}, \texttt{|=}, \texttt{\&=}, and
\texttt{\textasciicircum{}=}. Import these operators explicitly where
required; they are enabled for all enum types.

\section{Constexpr iteration, dispatch, fusion, and
navigation}\label{ch29-constexpr-iteration-dispatch-fusion-and-navigation}

\begin{code}
dsl::enum_for_each<Token>([](auto constant) {
  constexpr Token value = decltype(constant)::value;
  // Instantiate enum-specific code for each value.
});

auto integer = dsl::enum_switch([](auto constant) {
  return dsl::enum_integer(decltype(constant)::value);
}, Token::Identifier, -999);
\end{code}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \texttt{enum\_\allowbreak{}for\_\allowbreak{}each\textless{}\allowbreak{}E\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}fn)\allowbreak{}}
  invokes \texttt{fn} with each \texttt{enum\_\allowbreak{}constant}.
  Void-returning functions produce no result; homogeneous results
  produce an array, and heterogeneous results produce a tuple.
\item
  \texttt{enum\_\allowbreak{}switch(\allowbreak{}fn,\allowbreak{} value)\allowbreak{}}
  dispatches a runtime value into a compile-time constant. An unmatched
  value or unsupported handler receives a default-constructed result (or
  no action for \texttt{void}). The three-argument overload accepts an
  explicit fallback result. An explicit result type and reflection mode
  are supported by the upstream overloads.
\item
  \texttt{enum\_\allowbreak{}fuse(\allowbreak{}a,\allowbreak{} b,\allowbreak{} .\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{})\allowbreak{}}
  combines at least two reflected enum values into an optional,
  type-safe enum discriminator suitable for
  \texttt{switch}/\texttt{case}. All arguments must be reflected; the
  combined representation must fit in
  \texttt{std:\allowbreak{}:\allowbreak{}uintmax\_\allowbreak{}t}.
\item
  \texttt{enum\_\allowbreak{}next\_\allowbreak{}value(\allowbreak{}value,\allowbreak{} steps = 1)\allowbreak{}}
  and
  \texttt{enum\_\allowbreak{}prev\_\allowbreak{}value(\allowbreak{}value,\allowbreak{} steps = 1)\allowbreak{}}
  return optionals when moving through the sorted value sequence. They
  return empty optionals for unknown values or out-of-bounds movement.
\item
  \texttt{enum\_\allowbreak{}next\_\allowbreak{}value\_\allowbreak{}circular(\allowbreak{}value,\allowbreak{} steps = 1)\allowbreak{}}
  and
  \texttt{enum\_\allowbreak{}prev\_\allowbreak{}value\_\allowbreak{}circular(\allowbreak{}value,\allowbreak{} steps = 1)\allowbreak{}}
  wrap around the sequence. Their starting value must be reflected.
\end{itemize}

\section{Enum-indexed containers}\label{ch29-enum-indexed-containers}

\texttt{dsl:\allowbreak{}:\allowbreak{}containers} provides the full
upstream containers, iterators, comparison policies, and helper
functions:

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \texttt{array\textless{}\allowbreak{}E,\allowbreak{} T,\allowbreak{} Index = .\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}}:
  fixed-size storage indexed by enum values, with iterators, checked
  \texttt{at}, tuple access, comparisons, and
  \texttt{fill}/\texttt{swap};
\item
  \texttt{make\_\allowbreak{}array\textless{}\allowbreak{}E\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}values.\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{})\allowbreak{}},
  \texttt{to\_\allowbreak{}array\textless{}\allowbreak{}E\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}c\_\allowbreak{}array)\allowbreak{}},
  and
  \texttt{get\textless{}\allowbreak{}Value\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}(\allowbreak{}array)\allowbreak{}};
\item
  \texttt{bitset\textless{}\allowbreak{}E,\allowbreak{} Index = .\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}.\allowbreak{}\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}}:
  constexpr enum-indexed bits, proxy references, bitwise operations,
  \texttt{set}/\texttt{reset}/\texttt{flip}, queries, string and integer
  conversions; \texttt{raw\_\allowbreak{}access} distinguishes raw bit
  positions from enum values;
\item
  \texttt{set\textless{}\allowbreak{}E,\allowbreak{} Compare = std:\allowbreak{}:\allowbreak{}less\textless{}\allowbreak{}E\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}}:
  a compact set with enum-keyed insertion, erasure, lookup, bounds
  queries, and bidirectional iteration;
\item
  \texttt{name\_\allowbreak{}less\textless{}\allowbreak{}\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}},
  \texttt{name\_\allowbreak{}greater\textless{}\allowbreak{}\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}},
  \texttt{name\_\allowbreak{}less\_\allowbreak{}case\_\allowbreak{}insensitive},
  and
  \texttt{name\_\allowbreak{}greater\_\allowbreak{}case\_\allowbreak{}insensitive}:
  name-based comparison policies;
\item
  \texttt{default\_\allowbreak{}indexing\textless{}\allowbreak{}E\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}}
  and
  \texttt{comparator\_\allowbreak{}indexing\textless{}\allowbreak{}Compare\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}}:
  index mapping policies for arrays and bitsets.
\end{itemize}

\begin{code}
constexpr auto weights = dsl::containers::make_array<Token>(1, 10, 0);
static_assert(weights[Token::Identifier] == 10);

dsl::containers::bitset<Token> seen{Token::Number, Token::End};
dsl::containers::set<Token, dsl::containers::name_less<>> tokens_by_name;
tokens_by_name.insert(Token::Identifier);
\end{code}

Container positions use the reflected sequence, not the enum's raw
integer. Checked operations retain upstream exception behavior;
\texttt{MAGIC\_\allowbreak{}ENUM\_\allowbreak{}NO\_\allowbreak{}EXCEPTION}
selects aborting container checks.

\section{Streams and formatting}\label{ch29-streams-and-formatting}

\begin{code}
using dsl::iostream_operators::operator<<;
using dsl::iostream_operators::operator>>;
std::cout << Token::Identifier; // "Identifier"
\end{code}

Insertion prints reflected names, flag combinations, or the underlying
integer for unknown values. It also accepts optional enum values.
Extraction parses a name or flag combination and sets \texttt{failbit}
on failure, leaving the destination value intact.

If the standard library provides
\texttt{\textless{}\allowbreak{}format\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}} and
\texttt{\_\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}cpp\_\allowbreak{}lib\_\allowbreak{}format},
enum formatters are enabled automatically, including when
\texttt{MuDSL.\allowbreak{}hpp} is included first. They support string
formatting specifications and numeric fallback for unknown values.
\texttt{\{fmt\}} support is enabled when its headers are included before
\texttt{MuDSL.\allowbreak{}hpp}; it remains optional.

\begin{code}
#include <fmt/format.h> // Optional external formatter, included first.
#include "MuDSL.hpp"
// fmt::format("{}", value), std::format("{}", value)
\end{code}

\section{Compiler behavior and
provenance}\label{ch29-compiler-behavior-and-provenance}

Reflection uses upstream compiler-signature parsing
(\texttt{\_\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}PRETTY\_\allowbreak{}FUNCTION\_\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}}
or
\texttt{\_\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}FUNCSIG\_\allowbreak{}\_\allowbreak{}}).
It supports GCC, Clang, and MSVC on the versions supported by
magic\_enum; the surrounding MuDSL API requires C++20. Forward-declared
enums cannot be reflected. Alias naming is compiler-dependent, and
aliases do not add distinct values. Large scan intervals increase
constexpr compilation work. See the pinned upstream
\href{https://github.com/Neargye/magic_enum/blob/v0.9.8/doc/reference.md}{reference}
and
\href{https://github.com/Neargye/magic_enum/blob/v0.9.8/doc/limitations.md}{limitations}
for complete overload and compiler details.

The embedded block retains all upstream MIT copyright and permission
notices.
\texttt{scripts/\allowbreak{}update-magic-enu\allowbreak{}m.\allowbreak{}py}
recursively expands the public headers, preserves their include guards,
adds optional
\texttt{\textless{}\allowbreak{}format\textgreater{}\allowbreak{}}
detection, and defers container-specific string requirements until those
operations are used. This allows core reflection's minimal custom string
aliases to coexist with the included container declarations. Its source
digest pins the exact v0.9.8 headers. To reproduce or verify the block
from an upstream v0.9.8 checkout:

\begin{code}
python3 MuDSL/scripts/update-magic-enum.py /path/to/magic_enum
python3 MuDSL/scripts/update-magic-enum.py /path/to/magic_enum --check
\end{code}

The integration tests can be built independently of the other MetaTk
libraries:

\begin{code}
cmake -S MuDSL/tests -B build/mudsl-enums
cmake --build build/mudsl-enums
ctest --test-dir build/mudsl-enums --output-on-failure
\end{code}

The MetaTk build also enables these tests with
\texttt{BUILD\_\allowbreak{}TESTING=ON} and the example with
\texttt{BUILD\_\allowbreak{}EXAMPLES=ON}.
